WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.323
The read is straightforward:
at each governed scope,

2
00:00:03.323 --> 00:00:06.063
both schedule lists and
one policy per role.

3
00:00:06.063 --> 00:00:10.401
A schedule counts as permanently
active only when it's assigned,

4
00:00:10.401 --> 00:00:13.349
never ends, isn't an
activation, and is direct.

5
00:00:13.349 --> 00:00:15.300
The plan is where order matters.

6
00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:20.063
Policies go first, because a request
that breaks the policy is refused.

7
00:00:20.063 --> 00:00:22.274
New eligible assignments go second.

8
00:00:22.274 --> 00:00:24.646
And standing access is removed last,

9
00:00:24.646 --> 00:00:27.887
so nobody loses a role
before they can activate it.

10
00:00:27.887 --> 00:00:31.930
Anything eligible that the file
doesn't mention is reported,

11
00:00:31.930 --> 00:00:35.880
not removed: taking access away
is its own reviewed change.
